A||||5||86SE||New EGR valve - more problem arose.........||||8||
Z||000000||86SE||06-27-2000||08:25 PM||||Just bought and installed a new egr valve.  Its not like the stock one, I had to install some sort of 3/4" washer in the hole on the underside of the valve.  I took a wild guess of what one to pick (chances were 1/15) and put it in.  I dont think this is my problem, but anyway.....The idle now is perfect, stays right at about 950 RPM, little or no movement.   But now when I rev it - lets say I rev it to 3000 and see If I can hold it there.  I put it to 3000, (AC off and radio off (no load on the alt)), it stays at 3000 RPM for a second or 2, then it drops to 2700, then back up to 3000, then down to 2700, then back to 3000 and so on.........all this with keeping the petal still!!<P>I can unplug the vaccume line at the EGR valve with NO change in idle.<P>So far I re-pluged and unpluged the tach filter, switched ignition coil with a new coil, and unpluged the vaccume hose.  All with no change, it still drops by about 300 rpm any where above idle.<P>Any ideas?<BR>Thanks!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||loafer87gt||06-27-2000||08:39 PM||||A similar thing happened on my GT last week. It turned out my thottle linkage was gummed up from when I detailed my engine bay. I took some alcohol and poured it on the linkage and had someone inside the car press the gas pedal on and off and it cleaned the stuck throttle linkage. Whatever you do, Don't use WD40 to lubricate the cable, as it will attract more dust and really gum up your linkage. Hopefully this fixes your problem,||||reg||1
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||06-27-2000||08:45 PM||||I think you have the wrong washer installed. You must use the original part # for the EGR valve, then find the matching washer that goes with it (there should be installation instructions that comes with the new valve.)<BR>I recently installed one and I used the #11 (I think) washer based on part #17085897 for an 86GT 4spd. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||06-27-2000||09:20 PM||||WOW, im surprised, I happened to use the #11 washer too.  It did come with instructions, but  I couldent find a part number on the old one, i'll look again because I know there are 2 different EGR valves for the v6's.||||reg||3
Z||000004||86SE||06-28-2000||02:09 AM||||Well, that sure isnt the problem (unless it fell out). The washers are the same, I put in #11.  Hmmmmmm....||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||06-28-2000||09:54 PM||||The EGR valve does not work at idle speed, that Is why It idles ok. when you get to 3000 RPM and it bounces back and forth then It Is getting too much EGR. I really dont know what to tell you about the washers, but I would try a smaller one.||||reg||1
